    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0713" n="701" xml:id="pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79682/65</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 190</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-03">November 3,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received November 16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s Airgram No. A–22, July 26, 1943, and to state that, in my opinion,
                    there is little or no likelihood of obtaining for Pan American Airways and its
                    personnel the exemptions in Article 4 of the Defense Agreement of March 31,
                    1942, between the Government of the United States and the Government of Liberia,
                    because: (1) It is quite probable that the Government of Liberia would take the
                    position that such an amendment would become coterminous with the life of the
                    Agreement concluded between the Government of Liberia and Pan American Airways
                    on July 14, 1941; (2) It would appear that the Liberian Government is inclined
                    to believe that Pan American Airways is carrying others than members of the
                    armed forces and civilians whose transportation has been approved as essential
                    to the prosecution of the war.</p>
                <p>It has occurred to me that probably a temporary arrangement might be effectuated
                    designed to obtain for the duration the desired exemptions for Pan American
                    Airways and individual members of the Pan American Airways staff.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lester</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
